          prompt: 'Describe what happens during the electrolysis of molten sodium chloride (NaCl) using inert electrodes, including the half-reactions at each electrode.',
          answer:
            'At the cathode (negative electrode), sodium ions are reduced: Na⁺ + e⁻ → Na. At the anode (positive electrode), chloride ions are oxidised: 2Cl⁻ → Cl₂ + 2e⁻. Molten sodium metal collects at the cathode and chlorine gas is released at the anode.',
