          prompt: 'Use collision theory to explain why the rate of a reaction decreases as the reactants are gradually consumed and their concentration falls.',
          answer:
            'As reactant concentration decreases, there are fewer reactant particles per unit volume, so the frequency of collisions between reactant particles decreases. With fewer collisions occurring per unit time, fewer of them are effective (successful), so the reaction rate decreases.',
