          explanation: 'Since the gradient of a concentration-time graph at any point represents the (negative) reaction rate at that instant, the initially steep gradient reflects the fast rate when reactant concentration (and hence collision frequency) is highest, while the gradually flattening curve reflects the continuously decreasing rate as the reactant is consumed.',
