          explanation: 'The ability to hydrogen bond with water is the key factor that determines miscibility for organic compounds: smaller alcohols (with a proportionally larger −OH group relative to their non-polar carbon chain) tend to be highly miscible with water, while non-polar hydrocarbons like pentane are not.',
