          explanation: 'This is yet another classic illustration of the exceptional strength of hydrogen bonding, this time within group 15 of the periodic table (nitrogen’s group), mirroring the equivalent comparisons already seen for group 16 (water vs hydrogen sulfide) and group 17 (hydrogen fluoride vs the other hydrogen halides).',
