          answer: 'The enthalpy change (ΔH) of a reaction is the difference between the total energy of the products and the total energy of the reactants.',
          explanation: 'ΔH is negative for an exothermic reaction (products lower in energy than reactants) and positive for an endothermic reaction (products higher in energy than reactants).',
