          prompt: 'Define diffraction.',
          answer: 'Diffraction is the spreading out of a wave as it passes through a narrow gap (aperture) or around the edge of an obstacle.',
          explanation: 'Diffraction is a property shared by all types of waves, and becomes most noticeable when the size of the gap or obstacle is comparable to or smaller than the wavelength of the wave.',
