          explanation: 'This shows that diffraction around a small obstacle and diffraction through a narrow gap are explained by exactly the same underlying mechanism in Huygens’ principle — both depend on secondary wavelets, generated at points adjacent to an edge, spreading into a region that a purely straight-line (ray) picture would predict to be in shadow.',
