          answer: 'The enthalpy change, ΔH, of a reaction is the difference between the total energy of the products and the total energy of the reactants (ΔH = Hproducts − Hreactants).',
          explanation: 'A negative value of ΔH indicates an exothermic reaction (products have lower energy than reactants, so net energy is released), while a positive value of ΔH indicates an endothermic reaction (products have higher energy than reactants, so net energy is absorbed).',
