          explanation: 'This diagram visually captures the two key energy features of any reaction: the activation energy (the height of the "hump" that must be climbed) and the overall enthalpy change ΔH, which for an exothermic reaction is negative since the products end up lower in energy than the reactants, meaning the reaction releases net energy to the surroundings.',
