          answer: 'Examples include an electric bell, a relay, an electromagnetic crane (for lifting scrap metal), and a magnetic door lock. In a relay, for example, energising the solenoid magnetises its core, which attracts and pulls a metal lever/switch, closing (or opening) contacts in a separate, often higher-current, circuit.',
