          answer: 'The original two bulbs become dimmer (their brightness decreases, but they do not go out completely).',
          explanation: 'In a series circuit, the same current flows through every component. Adding a third bulb in series increases the total resistance of the circuit, which decreases the total current supplied by the battery (I = V ÷ Rtotal). Since all three bulbs share this same, now-smaller current, and brightness depends on the current through a bulb, the original two bulbs become dimmer than before the third bulb was added.',
