          prompt: 'Use the bond energies given to calculate the enthalpy change (ΔH) for this reaction, and state whether the reaction is exothermic or endothermic.',
          answer: 'ΔH = −542 kJ·mol⁻¹; the reaction is exothermic.',
          explanation: 'Energy needed to break bonds (reactants): (1 × H–H) + (1 × F–F) = 436 + 158 = 594 kJ·mol⁻¹. Energy released forming bonds (products): 2 × (H–F) = 2 × 568 = 1 136 kJ·mol⁻¹. ΔH = energy to break bonds − energy released forming bonds = 594 − 1 136 = −542 kJ·mol⁻¹. Since ΔH is negative, more energy is released forming the new bonds than was needed to break the original bonds, so the reaction is exothermic.',
