          explanation: 'In both diagrams, an activation-energy "hump" must still be climbed from the reactants before reaching the products, but whether the products end up higher or lower than the starting reactants (and hence the sign of ΔH) is what fundamentally distinguishes an endothermic reaction’s diagram from an exothermic reaction’s diagram.',
