          answer: 'Al: 0 → +3 (oxidised); Cu: +2 → 0 (reduced). Copper(II) sulfate (CuSO₄, via the Cu²⁺ ion) is the oxidising agent.',
          explanation: 'Aluminium’s oxidation number increases from 0 to +3 (loses electrons, is oxidised); copper’s oxidation number decreases from +2 to 0 (gains electrons, is reduced), making the Cu²⁺ ions (supplied by CuSO₄) the oxidising agent.',
