          answer: 'H₃PO₄(aq) + 3NaOH(aq) → Na₃PO₄(aq) + 3H₂O(l)',
          explanation: 'Phosphoric acid is triprotic (donates 3 protons per molecule), so it reacts with 3 formula units of the monoprotic base NaOH, producing sodium phosphate (Na₃PO₄) and water, with the equation balanced accordingly (3 NaOH and 3 H₂O needed to balance the sodium and the hydrogen/oxygen).',
