          prompt: 'Define the wavelength of a wave, in terms of successive wavefronts.',
          answer: 'The wavelength is the distance between two successive (adjacent) wavefronts that are in phase with each other — for example, the distance between one wavefront representing a crest and the very next wavefront also representing a crest.',
          explanation: 'Because all points along a single wavefront are in phase, the perpendicular spacing between consecutive wavefronts directly represents one full wavelength of the wave.',
