          explanation: 'This relationship is why reversing the direction of current flow through a motor’s coil at the correct moment (using a split-ring commutator, in a DC motor) is essential to keep the resulting force acting in a consistent rotational direction as the coil spins — without this periodic reversal, the force would simply reverse direction on its own as the coil rotates past a certain point, and continuous rotation could not be sustained.',
