          marks: 2,
          prompt: 'Define the term "transition state" (activated complex) in the context of a chemical reaction.',
          answer: 'The transition state (activated complex) is the unstable, high-energy, intermediate arrangement of atoms that exists momentarily at the peak of the energy "hump", as reactant bonds are breaking and product bonds are forming during a reaction.',
