          explanation: 'This diagram visually captures the two key energy features of any reaction: the activation energy (the height of the "hump" that must be climbed) and the overall enthalpy change ΔH (the net difference in height between reactants and products), which for an endothermic reaction is positive since the products end up higher in energy than the reactants.',
