          explanation: 'Energy needed to break bonds (reactants): (1 × H–H) + (1 × Br–Br) = 436 + 193 = 629 kJ·mol⁻¹. Energy released forming bonds (products): 2 × (H–Br) = 2 × 366 = 732 kJ·mol⁻¹. ΔH = energy to break bonds − energy released forming bonds = 629 − 732 = −103 kJ·mol⁻¹. Since ΔH is negative, more energy is released forming the new bonds than was needed to break the original bonds, so the reaction is exothermic.',
